Subject: Answer Loose Equality Between A Rope And A Flat String

What this does
  js_eq_slow sends two strings to js_strict_eq2 even when their tags differ, so a
  rope compared with a flat string takes the same-type path that === already
  takes.

Why we need it
  A rope (JS_TAG_STRING_ROPE) and a flat string (JS_TAG_STRING) are the same
  ECMAScript type, and ECMA-262 7.2.15 step 1 dispatches on type, not on tag. The
  tag equality test made `rope == flat` answer false while `rope === flat`
  answered true.

What it adds
  One condition: `tag1 == tag2 || (tag_is_string(tag1) && tag_is_string(tag2))`.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 5dbf1b6..18208ee 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -17692,7 +17692,8 @@ static no_inline __exception int js_eq_slow(JSContext *ctx, JSValue *sp,
             if (res < 0)
                 goto exception;
         }
-    } else if (tag1 == tag2) {
+    } else if (tag1 == tag2 ||
+               (tag_is_string(tag1) && tag_is_string(tag2))) {
         res = js_strict_eq2(ctx, op1, op2, JS_EQ_STRICT);
         JS_FreeValue(ctx, op1);
         JS_FreeValue(ctx, op2);
